SCHEDULE: {"1":"Ben","2":"Dev","3":"Cara","4":"Elif","5":"Hana","6":"Finn","7":"Ann","8":"Gus","9":"Ivo"}
CONFIDENCE: 97

Dev must be slot 2. Slot 1 is impossible: Elif would be slot 3, and Ben must be at least three slots from Elif and before her. Dev at 3 or higher leads to contradictions, so Dev is 2, which forces Elif to 4 and Ben to 1. Finn, Ann, Gus, and Ivo then fall into the chain Finn < Ann < Gus < Ivo, with Ivo = Gus + 1. Of the placements that remain, only Finn 6, Ann 7, Gus 8, Ivo 9 leaves Cara and Hana in slots 3 and 5 with the required gap of two. I checked all 17 constraints against this schedule and it satisfies them. I did not check every branch for other Dev values in full detail, so the 97 reflects that small gap.
